CRITERION 1 -- oracle passes, exit 0: **NOT MET**
  Run A (root), `cd /tmp/claude-0/f4-tests && bash .swarm/tier3/F4/accept.sh`:
      CHECK 01-migration-preserves-mode: PASS
      CHECK 02-package-suite-race: FAIL (want 0, got 1)
      FAIL  budget2/internal/services/storage  900.335s
      CHECK 03-build: PASS
      CHECK 04-vet: PASS
      passed=3 failed=1
  Run B (non-root `nobody`, same script, /tmp/claude-0/f4-nr):
      CHECK 01-migration-preserves-mode: PASS
      CHECK 02-package-suite-race: FAIL (want 0, got 1)
      FAIL  budget2/internal/services/storage  900.252s
      CHECK 03-build: PASS
      CHECK 04-vet: PASS
      passed=3 failed=1
  The oracle exits non-zero in both runs, so the criterion as written is not satisfied.
  What check 02 failed on, precisely:
    - Run B contains no `--- FAIL` line at all; the 900.252s figure is exactly the
      script's `-timeout 900s` budget, and the dump is a timeout goroutine trace
      (`.../storage/storage.go:418 encodeForWrite` mid-work), not a data race and not
      an assertion failure.
    - The same command with the brief's 1200s budget passes: as `nobody` in
      /tmp/claude-0/f4-nr, `go test -race -count=1 -timeout 1200s ./internal/services/storage/`
      -> "ok  budget2/internal/services/storage  1036.428s", race_exit=0. 1036s > the
      oracle's 900s budget on this 4-CPU, contended machine.
    - Run A (root) would have failed check 02 regardless of timing, because of the
      capability artifact described under criterion 6.
  Neither cause is attributable to F4's change: check 01, the check that tests F4's
  actual property, PASSED in both runs. Recorded as FAIL because the criterion asks for
  exit 0 and no run I made produced it; the lead adjudicates whether a 900s budget that
  this machine cannot meet counts against the task.

CRITERION 2 -- mode preservation end to end: **MET**
  Independent reproduction, not the worker's test: /tmp/claude-0/f4-e2e/cmd/permprobe
  (a small main.go using storage.New / EnableEncryption / DisableEncryption).
  `cd /tmp/claude-0/f4-e2e && go run ./cmd/permprobe`:
      BEFORE EnableEncryption:     -rw------- (octal 0600)
      AFTER  EnableEncryption:     -rw------- (octal 0600)
      AFTER  DisableEncryption:    -rw------- (octal 0600)
      content after round trip: "account,balance\nchecking,1.00\n"
  The probe demonstrably discriminates on this machine: the identical binary run in
  /tmp/claude-0/f4-m1 (encryptFileWithRecipient reverted to atomicWrite(..., 0644)) gives
      BEFORE EnableEncryption:     -rw------- (octal 0600)
      AFTER  EnableEncryption:     -rw-r--r-- (octal 0644)
      AFTER  DisableEncryption:    -rw-r--r-- (octal 0644)
  i.e. the historical bug exactly as the report describes it, so the 0600/0600 result
  above is a real measurement and not root ignoring modes.

CRITERION 3 -- each of the four helpers independently defended: **MET**
  Four hand mutations, one per helper, each on its own scratch copy of the merged tree
