SUMMARY
  Criteria 2, 3, 4, 6 are demonstrated by commands whose output is quoted above; the
  substance of F4 -- all four helpers preserve the mode, each defended by its own direct
  test, with the 0644-stays-0644 guard that blocks the hardcode-0600 cheat -- holds up
  under independent reproduction and six hand mutations.
  Criterion 1 is not met: the oracle exits 1 in both a root and a non-root run, on check
  02 only, which is the nested regression guard (package suite under -race, 900s budget)
  and not F4's own check. Non-root the failure is a pure timeout at 900.252s on a 4-CPU
  contended machine; the identical command at the brief's 1200s budget passes with
  exit 0 and no races.
  Criterion 5's code is correct but no test or oracle check would catch a
  `return 0644, nil` fallback (mutant m5 passes the entire suite plus the oracle tests).
